    "note": "analyze.py implements the BENCHMARK.md selection rule over raw/samples.jsonl (per-call elapsed_ns/reps; medians and observed ranges across 12 blocks; paired [min, median, max] ratios; lowest median leader, unique only when every rival/leader ratio exceeds 1.05) and emits the RESULTS.json cell schema. It was added after the campaigns; the committed RESULTS.json was derived by an uncommitted analysis step and has not yet been regenerated from the archived samples with this script. analyze.py rejects any samples file that lacks the complete runner.py schedule (11 cells x 12 blocks x 4 candidates at their scheduled positions); test_analyze.py covers that rejection with synthetic samples.",
